 ## Operating characteristics
 **Time and Memory Complexity**
-- **Memory**: The memory footprint is proportional to the number of SH coefficients per sample. For degree $L$, there are $(L+1)^2$ coefficients per channel, so $3(L+1)^2$ coefficients per sample. This is significantly less than storing full RGB values if the angular variation is smooth and can be well-approximated by low-degree SH [S1, S2, unofficial].
-- **Time**: The time complexity is dominated by the evaluation of the SH basis functions and the dot product with the coefficients. For degree $L$, the basis evaluation is $O(L^2)$ per sample, and the dot product is $O(L^2)$ per sample. This is generally faster than evaluating complex lighting models per sample [S1, S2, unofficial].
+Memory usage scales with the number of SH coefficients per sample. For band limit $b$, there are $(b+1)^2$ coefficients per channel, totaling $3(b+1)^2$ coefficients per sample [S1, unofficial]. Time complexity is dominated by the evaluation of the SH basis functions and the dot product with the coefficients [S2, S3, unofficial].
 
