 **Strengths and Limitations**
-- **Strengths**: Compact representation of view-dependent effects; efficient to evaluate; suitable for real-time rendering if precomputed [S1, S2, unofficial].
-- **Limitations**: Limited angular resolution for high-frequency details; requires precomputation or training to obtain coefficients; may not capture sharp specularities well with low degrees [S1, S2, unofficial].
+Strengths include a compact representation of view-dependent effects and reduced memory overhead compared to storing full RGB tensors per sample [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. Limitations include the inability to capture high-frequency angular details when using low band limits [S1, unofficial].
 
 **When to Use**
-- Use when view-dependent effects are important and memory is constrained [S1, S2, unofficial].
-- Use when the lighting can be well-approximated by low-degree SH [S1, S2, unofficial].
