 ## Background
-Spherical Harmonics Rendering is used in the context of neural radiance fields (NeRF) and implicit surface representations to model view-dependent shading [S1, S2, unofficial]. It was popularized by works such as "NeRF--Representing Scenes as Neural Radiance Fields for View Synthesis" and subsequent extensions that incorporate SH for view-dependent effects [S1, S2, unofficial]. The method is implemented in frameworks like Nerfstudio and SDFStudio [S1, S2, unofficial].
+Spherical Harmonics Rendering is used in neural radiance fields and implicit surface representations to model view-dependent shading [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. It was popularized by works such as "NeRF--Representing Scenes as Neural Radiance Fields for View Synthesis" and subsequent extensions incorporating SH for view-dependent effects [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. The method is implemented in frameworks like Nerfstudio and SDFStudio [S2, S3, unofficial].
 
